[gd_scene load_steps=13 format=3]

; ─────────────────────────────────────────────
; GEORGETOWN — THE GAMEPLAY LAYER, AS ITS OWN SCENE.
;
; WHY THIS IS NOT IN maps/georgetown_level.tscn. That file is WRITTEN BY
; tools/build_georgetown.gd. Its _write_level() emits the whole thing as text
; from a template, so every hand-added node in it is destroyed by the next
; --force rebuild — which is how the Hillfort's relay and extraction went
; missing and shipped a mission with a blank objective HUD.
;
; So the level holds exactly ONE line of gameplay: an instance of this scene.
; Re-applying it after a rebuild is tools/mission_ops.sh, which is two lines
; of insertion and nothing else. Everything a mission names lives here, in a
; file the terrain tools do not know about and cannot overwrite.
;
; EVERY POSITION IN HERE HAS BEEN WALKED, not eyeballed:
;   LEVEL=res://maps/georgetown_level.tscn godot --headless --audio-driver Dummy \
;       --path . --script res://tools/probe_mission_anchors.gd
; snaps each one to the baked navmesh and paths to it from the spawn. A post on
; an island is a garrison that stands still for the whole operation and nothing
; says so, which is the single most expensive authoring mistake on this map.
;
; TWO THINGS THE BAKE DECIDES AND THIS SCENE HAS TO RESPECT:
;
;   1. THE TOWN STOPS AT z = -140. The town bench is tiled back to z = -264,
;      but the navmesh's filter_baking_aabb starts at -140, so the modern
;      office block (z = -180) and the whole north third of the bench have no
;      walkable ground on them. Nothing up there can be a post, an objective or
;      an extraction.
;   2. THE RIVER EDGE STOPS AT z = +160. The piers and the boathouse run out to
;      z = 186 and are off the mesh — which is why TERRAIN's own GT_Pier pin
;      reads 6.5 m off it. The esplanade at 162 is the last walkable line.
;
; THE SHAPE OF THE OPERATION. Four flat benches, 14 m of fall between the top
; and the river, and the only ways between them are stairs, two ramped streets
; and the canal crossings. So the mission is a climb, and each bench is a
; stage with its own relay:
;
;   WHARF   z +116..+226, y -8   the derelict park. You come ashore here.
;   YARDS   z  +46..+106, y -4   the industrial level. The stack is on it.
;   CANAL   z    0,       y  0   the cut. Five crossings, one of them a lock.
;   TOWN    z -140..-48,  y +4   rowhouses either side of one street.
;
; Up through all four, and out the east end of the upper street — so the
; operation crosses the map diagonally rather than straight up it, and uses
; every bench's full length instead of one stair on each.
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────

[ext_resource type="PackedScene" uid="uid://g7fmy28elpah" path="res://Env/world_objects/spawn_point.tscn" id="1_spawn"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://Campaign/squad_spawn_point.gd" id="2_squad"]
